<title>GERMANY: German farm minister backs transgenic food labels.</title>
<headline>German farm minister backs transgenic food labels.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonn government supports a comprehensive and practicable labelling scheme for genetically-modified foods, farm minister Jochen Borchert said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The consumer should have the last word on the use of biotechnology,&quot; he said at the opening ceremony of the ANUGA FoodTec trade fair.</p>
<p>But Germany must not opt out of the responsible uses of biotechnology, which offered growth opportunities in agricultural and food industries, he said.</p>
<p>The first new crop soybean shipment from the U.S., possibly containing gene-modified beans, is due to arrive in Germany on Tuesday.</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40741903275</p>
